From 83c2887e111bf15a9b1e614ce6354a07bd3af48a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Lane A <lane-a@local.invalid>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 22:56:34 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 10/22] fix(reaction): pass Sanji's fixture decoy: mic channel,
 screams, face, coincidence

Fixture v2 (decoy: loudest explosion, still face, silent mic) ranked
the decoy #1 because no reaction episode formed and the fallback ranked
game events by strength alone. Measured causes and fixes, each behind a
switch:

- Split stereo is read on the mic channel (L/R corr 0.0 on the fixture;
  real streams mix the mic into both channels, corr ~1, unchanged).
  REACTION_MIC_CHANNEL.
- Face activity is measured on the YuNet face patch (expression change
  plus head travel vs face size) instead of the whole facecam rectangle,
  whose background dominated. REACTION_FACE_ACTIVITY=roi restores it.
- REACTION_FUSION: a scream (pitch z >= 4 with vocal z >= 1.5) counts;
  on a known mic channel the streamer's own top-1 % loudest seconds with
  a raised voice are bursts (per-task, contract s3); a laugh pulse needs
  the voice raised in that second; unreacted game events rank by
  coincidence = min(sqrt(event / task max), reaction level), and only
  those with coincidence >= 0.25 survive next to real reactions.

Fixture v2 (tools/phase2/score_fixture.py): 6/7 checks PASS (R3 #1, R1
second with its setup, decoy out); R2 still missed (no measurable face
or game event there). Synthetic VOD matrix (score_streamer.py vod_v1):
positives 2/5 -> 5/5; the one negative ranks last (6th of 6, score 14
vs 21 for the weakest positive). 38 reaction tests pass.

Also: gate_compare.py resolves its output path before changing directory.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
